  <!--
    NOTE FOR NEXT DEV SESSION:
    index.html is a single-page app that routes via URL hash
    (e.g. /#library, /#blog/income-tax-2025), not via server-side
    paths. Flask's catch-all route always returns the same index.html
    regardless of path, so a crawler hitting /qa-library or
    /blog/income-tax-2025 directly gets the homepage, not the
    targeted page/article — the JS never reads location.pathname.
    Until routing is made server-aware (e.g. server returns page-specific
    <title>/meta tags per path, or the app migrates to real path-based
    routing), these entries mainly serve as a discovery hint to crawlers
    and the entries below use hash fragments to at least match what a
    user's browser will actually resolve to.
  -->

